-- title:
--   Membership in the finite part of a Néron extension
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime and nonzero, together with a proof $h_{pN_0}$ that $p \nmid N_0$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the `AlgebraicClosure` of $\mathbb{Q}$) satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $N_0$, $p$, $A$ (a section $\sigma_A$ of the base over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lifting the generic point, a scheme $X$ over the base with a relative group law, and identifications of $J_0(N_0)$ and of its reduction with the generic- and residual-fibre points), and let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, i.e. a smooth separated commutative group scheme $g \colon G \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ with all its listed properties, whose generic-fibre points are identified with $J_0(N_0p) := \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field at level $N_0p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $F$ be a `NeronExtension` of $O$, let $m$ be a natural number and let $x \in J_0(N_0p)$. Then $x$ lies in the subgroup $F.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ — by definition the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by those $y$ which are killed by $m$ (lie in `Submodule.torsionBy ℤ _ (m : ℤ)`) and satisfy $F.\mathrm{ExtN}\,y$, the existence of a section $s$ of $F.g_N$ over $\mathrm{shPt}\,A$ with $F.\mathrm{ptsN}\,y$ equal to $\mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by $s$ — if and only if $x$ is itself $m$-torsion and satisfies $F.\mathrm{ExtN}\,x$.
--
--   The statement records that the generating set of the finite part $F.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ is already a subgroup, so that membership in it is the conjunction of $m$-torsion with the condition that the associated point of the Néron extension spreads out to a section over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the strictly henselian base. It serves as the unfolding lemma used when comparing the finite part with a Hopf-algebra description of the $m$-torsion and when verifying inclusions of subgroups into $F.\mathrm{finPts}$ pointwise.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_NeronExtension_mem_finPts_iff.lean

